verses.raw_usfm:
There is a reproof that is not timely;  
\q2 and there is a person who is wise enough to keep silent.   
\q1

There is one who keeps silent and is found wise;  
\q2 and there is one who is hated for his much talk.   
\q1

There is one who keeps silent, for he has no answer to make;  
\q2 And there is one who keeps silent, knowing when to speak.   
\q1

There is a prosperity that a man finds in misfortunes;  
\q2 and there is a gain that turns to loss.   
\q1

There is a gift that will not profit you;  
\q2 and there is a gift that pays back double.   
\q1

There are losses because of glory;  
\q2 and there is one who has lifted up his head from a low estate.   
\q1

He who is wise in words will make himself beloved;  
\q2 but the pleasantries of fools will be wasted.   
\q1
